Source-data provenance
----------------------

The packaged database paths, original sizes, and SHA-256 checksums are
recorded in packaged_files.json. NIST_SRD46_core_db_storage/README.md
describes the database contents. Dated source-processing notes and the
original data terms are preserved in
NIST_SRD46_core_db_storage/NIST_SRD46_database_parsing/_input/SRD46_SQL/SRD 46 README.md.
Publication packaging preserves the database bytes and all archived run files.

The project parses the source SQL/text extraction, applies documented
chemical interpretation and correction rules, preserves identifiers and
provenance, and constructs four SQLite databases: srd46_cards.db,
srd46_equilibrium_maps.db, srd46_literature.db, and
srd46_ligand_fingerprints.db. The last database contains calculated RDKit
fingerprints and similarity scores. PubChem enrichment and QupKake pKa
estimates are separately identified. Predicted values and heuristic
protonation windows are project calculations, not NIST-selected
measurements. This processing statement describes the transformation of
source data for the initial release.

NIST's README identifies the SQL representation as an outside group's
extraction, whose reliability NIST does not guarantee, and reports known
errors in its structure database. This independent project is not endorsed
or certified by NIST. Preserve review flags and consult the scientific
sources when an unresolved interpretation affects a result.

